@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Summary of the repo changes (the real work lives in coding_agent.py and tools/stress_test.py):
+# 1. tools/stress_test.py: on mismatch, shrink by retrying seeds with generator size 1..max_size
+#    and report the smallest failing input with brute/solution raw outputs.
+# 2. coding_agent.py: _run_checks() (sample_check + stress_test when /work/scratch/brute.py and gen.py exist),
+#    bounded loop of at most 4 rounds, differential debugging in round 1, fresh-context re-derivation
+#    (msg_history=[]) when the same failure persists, tie-break hint only for 'any valid'/'multiple' statements.
+# 3. Empty-reply guard in _chat(): re-prompt with a short message containing the failing report.
+# 4. Best-solution backup in scratch/best_solution.py, restored at the end if the final version is worse.
+# 5. Prompts tell the agent to use only the standard library (no numpy).
